WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.163
Eleven checks.

2
00:00:01.163 --> 00:00:04.571
For the compliant network:
the named location exists,

3
00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:09.761
which tells you signaling was turned on;
the policy blocks everything outside it;

4
00:00:09.761 --> 00:00:13.247
the emergency group and both
Intune apps are excluded;

5
00:00:13.247 --> 00:00:16.732
no Private Access app is in
scope; while it's report-only,

6
00:00:16.732 --> 00:00:19.676
the business days and
the defects are counted,

7
00:00:19.676 --> 00:00:24.401
as information until it's ready; and once
it's enforced, signaling must be on.

8
00:00:24.401 --> 00:00:28.718
For tenant restrictions: the default
blocks everyone and everything;

9
00:00:28.718 --> 00:00:33.484
each partner allowance is in the register
and current; tagging is on only with

10
00:00:33.484 --> 00:00:38.160
a blocking default; and each blocked
tenant is listed for the weekly review.
